LOK: find Visual Studio 2026, which no longer registers the old component

The build looks for the compiler with vswhere and asks for
Microsoft.VisualStudio.Component.VC.Tools.x86.x64. Visual Studio 2026
does not register that id, so every query comes back empty and the build
stops with "no Visual Studio 2026 installation found" -- even though the
compiler is there.

When the year is 2026, ask for the product itself.  A Visual Studio in a
folder whose name has a space cannot be used at all (the build would need
the short names, which may be turned off), so the build may hand over a
path of its own through ELY_VS_ALIAS; that path is used as it is.
diff --git a/configure.ac b/configure.ac
index 9f67ee4..2d65f9f 100644
--- a/configure.ac
+++ b/configure.ac
@@ -4515,6 +4515,22 @@ find_msvc()
         if test -z "$vswhereoutput"; then
             vswhereoutput=`$vswhere -prerelease -version "@<:@ $ver , $(expr ${ver%%.*} + 1) @:}@" -requires Microsoft.VisualStudio.Component.VC.Tools.x86.x64 -property installationPath | head -1`
         fi
+        # Visual Studio 2026 does not register the old component id, so the
+        # queries above find nothing.  Ask for the product itself; the checks
+        # that follow look for the compiler and the Windows SDK, and they
+        # decide whether the installation is usable.  A path with a space in
+        # it cannot be used at all, so the build may hand over a path of
+        # its own; that one is taken as it is.
+        if test -z "$vswhereoutput" && test -n "$ELY_VS_ALIAS"; then
+            vswhereoutput="$ELY_VS_ALIAS"
+        fi
+        if test -z "$vswhereoutput"; then
+            case "$ver" in
+            18 | 18.0)
+                vswhereoutput=`$vswhere -products \* -version "@<:@ $ver , $(expr ${ver%%.*} + 1) @:>@" -property installationPath | head -1`
+                ;;
+            esac
+        fi
         # Fall back to all MS products (this includes VC++ Build Tools)
         if ! test -n "$vswhereoutput"; then
             AC_MSG_CHECKING([VC++ Build Tools and similar])
@@ -4541,6 +4557,14 @@ find_msvc()
             vcyear=2026
             vctoolset=v145
         esac
+        # A newer toolset may be installed with only its auxiliary files,
+        # so take the one that has the compiler.
+        for toolset in `ls $vctest/VC/Tools/MSVC -A1r`; do
+            if test -f "$vctest/VC/Tools/MSVC/$toolset/bin/Hostx64/x64/cl.exe"; then
+                vcbuildnumber=$toolset
+                break
+            fi
+        done
         vcbuildnumber=`ls $vctest/VC/Tools/MSVC -A1r | head -1`
 
     fi
